     Both the the show-experience and show-running-score options are
controlled by compile time options.  If compiled into the game, then
their actual display is controlled by run-time options which can be
set in your environment or toggled during play via the 'O' command.
The default configuration of the distributed sources includes show-
experience and excludes show-score.  If your binaries didn't have the
show-experience option available, it wouldn't have shown up in the
options help...

     Personally, I feel that the `time', `showexp', and `showscore'
status line values give too-much/too-specific information to the player
that his/her character wouldn't know, so I leave them off when I play.
I used to keep the experience points displayed, but found that it was
influencing my decisions during play.



